In one sparse-marker task, demonstrations showed output color 2 added along an axis-aligned rectangular perimeter determined by the extrema of marker positions, with original markers preserved and the rectangle's interior left unchanged. The initial hypotheses—vertical gap filling and filling every row/column span—were wrong. Treat frame construction as a candidate, not a default rule: confirm each edge and non-edge against all demonstrations, especially where marker positions extend beyond one another. For a candidate frame, compute min/max row and column over the relevant markers, color only the perimeter cells, and preserve existing markers.

